asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 389 69397 1292 20 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 389 69510 1293 64 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#396
|  With proper edge-filtering, tree "visiting"
.  algorithms (e.g., push/transfer) can be adopted to parse graphs
asl-sentence-text $# 396 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 390 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 390 69511 1293 65 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 390 69643 1296 21 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#397
|  Type-checking may be described as a graph-traversal
|  strategy where the "program stack" holds types rather
.  than concrete values
asl-sentence-text $# 397 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 391 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 391 69644 1296 22 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 391 69947 1302 9 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#398
|  Assuming
|  polymorphism, a type-checker
|  must confirm that, given any stack-state with a
|  procedure symbol on top, there is a unique implementation
|  whose parameter-types match those symbolized lower on the stack
|  (if so, its output type is then placed on the stack
.  instead)
asl-sentence-text $# 398 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 392 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 392 69948 1302 10 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 392 70414 1310 67 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#399
|  Both type-checking
|  and push/transfer may thereby be modeled
|  as versions of a generic graph-traversal pattern, whose
|  central operations are crossing to unvisited child nodes;
|  pushing leaf-nodes' values (or types, etc.) onto an
|  external stack; and performing some external operation
|  on non-leaf nodes once all descendent branches have been explored
|  (in effect, navigating graphs with a state
.  machine holding stack-memory and a trace of previously-seen nodes)
asl-sentence-text $# 399 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 392 70415 1310 68 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 393 ;.
asl-sentence-start-pos 4#/4 393 70417 1312 1 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 393 70734 1317 39 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#400
|  In short, whenever a directed graph models a computational
|  process, we can extract a postordering of nodes
|  representing the proper sequence for a push/transfer traversal;
|  and we can type-check relationships between
|  child nodes and parent nodes, the latter being interpreted
.  as procedures with specific signatures
asl-sentence-text $# 400 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 394 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 394 70735 1317 40 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 394 70860 1319 52 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#401
|  I believe
|  both of these operations --- postordering and type-checking
.  --- have approximate correlates in natural language
asl-sentence-text $# 401 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 395 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 395 70861 1319 53 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 395 71044 1323 47 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#402
|  The mapping of a general parse-graph onto
|  a postorder traversal sequence recalls
|  underlying machineries for conceptual synthesis,
.  conformant to a word-by-word "staging" order
asl-sentence-text $# 402 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 396 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 396 71045 1323 48 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 396 71327 1329 63 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#403
|  Intuitively, nouns are akin to
|  "values" pushed onto a conceptual stack,
|  whereas verbs, adjectives, and other modifiers
|  embody cognitive transforms applied to concepts
|  currently residing on this "stack"
.  (albeit which, in the present context, is mostly metaphorical)
asl-sentence-text $# 403 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 397 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 397 71328 1329 64 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 397 71491 1332 66 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#404
|  Given this conceptual background, I will adopt the
|  phrase "staging order" as a linguistic
.  counterpart to computational "push/transfer" order
asl-sentence-text $# 404 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 397 71492 1332 67 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 398 ;.
