$.#578
|  My arguments in this paper are that such an overly-tidy picture is
.  untenable
asl-sentence-text $# 578 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 574 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 574 104042 1963 11 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 574 104136 1964 46 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#579
|  Concepts simply don't synthesize according to
.  "production rules" akin to BNF grammars
asl-sentence-text $# 579 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 574 104137 1964 47 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 575 ;.
asl-sentence-start-pos 4#/4 575 104141 1966 1 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 575 104370 1970 6 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#580
|  I think the story  and many similar analyses have
|  in mind --- once expressed informally --- is roughly like this:
|  semantics tells us how to combine concepts;
|  syntax tells us which concepts to combine, in which
.  order
asl-sentence-text $# 580 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 576 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 576 104371 1970 7 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 576 104649 1975 54 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#581
|  I mostly dispute the first part; although
|  semantics establishes parameters on concept-admixture,
|  our intellect molds multi-part
|  conceptual formations against dictates
|  of social norms and purposeful action, rather than
.  by manipulating concepts as formalizable abstractions
asl-sentence-text $# 581 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 576 104650 1975 55 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 577 ;.
asl-sentence-start-pos 4#/4 577 104652 1977 1 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 577 105011 1983 9 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#582
|  To draw once again from coding analogies,
|  programming language semantics is concerned with the binding
|  of values to symbols --- when those "markings" start and
|  cease to be appropriate --- as well as polymorphic
|  definition of multiple procedures with thesymbol
|  but different parameter types, and other type-related
.  concerns
asl-sentence-text $# 582 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 578 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 578 105012 1983 10 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 578 105339 1988 21 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#583
|  Code syntax addresses such issues as
|  expression boundaries, storage-duration scope, and "sequence points", indicating
|  which values are parameters for which function-calls as
|  well as, potentially, the order of procedures' side-effects
|  (particularly when a prior effect could be "visible" to
.  a future subroutine)
asl-sentence-text $# 583 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 579 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 579 105340 1988 22 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 579 105563 1991 63 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#584
|  Syntactic and
|  semantic systems are necessary to ensure that high-level code
|  maps (properly) to a "push/transfer"-like stack representation, ensuring that
.  all procedures' type and precondition contracts are guaranteed
asl-sentence-text $# 584 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 580 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 580 105564 1991 64 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 580 105785 1995 46 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#585
|  Note that the algorithmetized syntax and semantics here
|  serve as preparation for function-calls, many of which
|  may be to precompiled routines whose implementations are
.  opaque to the high-level compiler and runtime
asl-sentence-text $# 585 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 581 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 581 105786 1995 47 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 581 106010 1999 44 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#586
|  I find this
|  roughly comparable to the role of syntax and semantics
|  in natural language, which bridge discourse to cognitive
|  operations even if the cognitive processing itself
.  is opaque to linguistic analysis per se
asl-sentence-text $# 586 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 581 106011 1999 45 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 582 ;.
asl-sentence-start-pos 4#/4 582 106014 2001 1 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 582 106163 2003 12 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#587
|  This exposition might be a little straw-man-like in that ,
|  for example, do not specifically work from a system of grammatical
.  productions
asl-sentence-text $# 587 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 583 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 583 106164 2003 13 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 583 106335 2005 57 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#588
|  Their syntactic theory is more about, starting
|  from any given sentence, retracing the compositional principles
.  that build up a complex network from isolated word-pairs
asl-sentence-text $# 588 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 584 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 584 106336 2005 58 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 584 106455 2007 45 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#589
|  We aren't "producing" (or, for that matter, "testing") sentences
.  so much as retracing their unifying formulae
asl-sentence-text $# 589 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 585 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 585 106456 2007 46 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 585 106601 2010 35 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#590
|  But still,
|  any analysis wherein conceptual syntheses
|  reciprocate composition-patterns implicitly invokes a
.  principle of conceptual production
asl-sentence-text $# 590 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 586 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 586 106602 2010 36 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 586 107008 2016 57 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#591
|  Either we view such production as inherently cognitive and extralinguistic, which is
|  my approach, or we must articulate rules for how concepts
|  in their totality form a logical system, wherein all concepts are
|  built up (almost syntactically!) from primitive roots by operations such as
|  those of set theory (union, intersection, disjoint union ...)
.  or other formalizations (modal logic, quantifiers, etc.)
asl-sentence-text $# 591 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 586 107009 2016 58 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 587 ;.
asl-sentence-start-pos 4#/4 587 107014 2018 1 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 587 107190 2020 65 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#592
|  Referring back to my reading of the successive syntheses
|  connoted by "in this red tin box", I don't believe
.  any of those transforms can be glossed in such logical terms
asl-sentence-text $# 592 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 588 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 588 107191 2020 66 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 588 107457 2025 19 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#593
|  Put aphoristically, linguistic formalization should model
|  --- perhaps with the aid of computational analogs --- processes
|  through which surface-level discourse is mapped to a sequence
|  of cognitive transforms presented to extralinguistic
.  rational faculties
asl-sentence-text $# 593 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 589 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 589 107458 2025 20 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 589 107587 2028 9 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#594
|  This is different from attempting
|  to model concept-synthesis, as a kind of
|  "algorithmetizable" cognitive process,
.  directly
asl-sentence-text $# 594 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 590 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 590 107588 2028 10 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 590 107777 2030 68 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#595
|  As a useful analogy, programmers are not obligated to
|  study how system-kernel procedures are implemented; they merely
.  need to know the type-signatures and preconditions for calling them
asl-sentence-text $# 595 ;.
asl-sentence-end-pos 4#/4 590 107778 2030 69 ;.

